      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe Rust frontend's model retrieval route matches only a single path segment. Requests such as `/v1/models/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B` therefore return 404 even when the served model ID exactly matches `Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`.\n\nThe Python frontend already supports model IDs containing slashes through its [`/v1/models/{model:path}` ](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/ed0b8f433f/python/sglang/srt/entrypoints/http_server.py#L1961) route.\n\n## Modifications\n\nChange the Axum route from `/v1/models/{model}` to `/v1/models/{*model}` to capture the full model ID.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: this change only affects HTTP routing.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Validation\n\nStarted the Rust frontend with `--served-model-name Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B`. The model ID was confirmed through `/v1/models`.\n```\nSGLANG_RUST_SERVER=1 \\\npython -m sglang.launch_server \\\n  --model-path /workplace/model/Qwen3-0.6B \\\n  --served-model-name Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B \\\n  --host 127.0.0.1 \\\n  --port 30002 \n```\n\n\n### Before\n\nThe model is listed by `/v1/models`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:30002/v1/models\n```\n\n```json\n{\"object\":\"list\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\",\"object\":\"model\",\"created\":1792410590,\"owned_by\":\"sglang\",\"root\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\",\"parent\":null,\"max_model_len\":4096}]}\n```\n\nRetrieving that same model returns an empty 404 response:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i http://127.0.0.1:30002/v1/models/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\n```\n\n```http\nHTTP/1.1 404 Not Found\ncontent-length: 0\n```\n\n### After\n\nRetrieving the model succeeds:\n\n```bash\ncurl -i http://127.0.0.1:30002/v1/models/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\n```\n\n```http\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\ncontent-type: application/json\ncontent-length: 142\n\n{\"id\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\",\"object\":\"model\",\"created\":1792411600,\"owned_by\":\"sglang\",\"root\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B\",\"parent\":null,\"max_model_len\":4096}\n```\n\nAn unknown model ID containing a slash reaches the model lookup handler and returns a JSON error:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s http://127.0.0.1:30002/v1/models/Qwen/missing\n```\n\n```json\n{\"error\":{\"object\":\"error\",\"message\":\"The model `Qwen/missing` does not exist\",\"type\":\"BadRequestError\",\"param\":null,\"code\":404}}\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (No unit tests added yet.)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (Not applicable: this fix restores model retrieval compatibility with the Python frontend and introduces no new user-facing API or configuration options.)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (Not applicable: this change only affects HTTP route matching for model retrieval.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39265603018](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39265603018)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39265603223](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39265603223)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
